                <head>265. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On August 3 at 11:30 a.m., President Johnson called an impromptu press conference at the White House
                    and read the following statement:</p>
                <p>“I have instructed the Navy: <list>
                        <item>“1. to continue the patrols in the Gulf of Tonkin off the coast of
                            North Viet-Nam,</item>
                        <item>“2. to double the force by adding an additional destroyer to the one
                            already on patrol</item>
                        <item>“3. to provide a combat air patrol over the destroyers, and</item>
                        <item>“4. to issue orders to the commanders of the combat aircraft and the
                            two destroyers, (a) to attack any force which attacks them in
                            international waters, and (b) to attack with the objective not only of
                            driving off the force but of destroying it.” (Department of State <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 24, 1964, page 259)</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
